    "rich_text_rLkyTp": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "richtext_kEMfkt": {
          "type": "richtext",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>Left vs. right hand, what each placement signals, and how to choose the right finger for your promise. A promise ring can be worn on any finger, but in the United States, the left ring finger and right ring finger are the most common choices.</p><p>If your promise ring represents a step toward a future engagement, wearing it on the left ring finger can feel the most natural. If you want the ring to symbolize romantic commitment without people assuming you are engaged, the right ring finger is often the clearest choice.</p><p>Middle and index fingers are also great options, particularly for <a href=\"https://thepromiseco.com/collections/friendship-rings\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https://thepromiseco.com/collections/friendship-rings\">friendship rings</a>, self-promise rings, relationships without marriage plans, or anyone who simply prefers a more modern look.</p><p><em><strong>QUICK ANSWER  </strong></em>There is no official promise-ring finger. Choose the left ring finger for a stronger pre-engagement meaning, the right ring finger for commitment without the engagement signal, or another finger when it better reflects your promise, personal style, or daily life.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "richtext_kEMfkt"
      ],
      "name": "t:sections.rich_text.presets.rich_text.name",
      "settings": {
        "color_scheme": "scheme-2",
        "separate_section_with_border": true,
        "content_width": "sm",
        "text_position": "center",
        "remove_vertical_spacing": false,
        "use_baka_too_font": false,
        "use_ogg_font": false,
        "use_compact_spacing": false,
        "section_id": ""
      }
    },
    "image_with_text_B6D4Yt": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "subheading_jLWbCG": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "text": "promise rings"
          }
        },
        "heading_LiTEN6": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "text": "What Finger Does a Promise Ring Go On?",
            "heading_tag": "h1"
          }
        },
        "richtext_hfT7Lx": {
          "type": "richtext",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>Unlike an engagement ring or wedding band, a promise ring does not come with a single established rule about where it has to be worn.</p><p>The Gemological Institute of America (GIA) recognizes several common placements, including the left ring finger, left middle finger, right middle finger, and right ring finger.</p><p>That flexibility reflects what a promise ring actually is. An engagement ring usually communicates one very specific message: we intend to get married. A promise ring can mean many different things.</p><p>•   A serious romantic relationship</p><p>•   Exclusivity between two partners</p><p>•  A future intention to become engaged</p><p>•  Long-term commitment without plans to marry</p><p>•  Staying connected during a long-distance relationship</p><p>•  Friendship</p><p>•  A promise made to yourself</p><p>Because the meaning varies, the best finger can vary too.</p>"
          }
        },
        "button_wBjPfw": {
          "type": "button",
          "settings": {
            "style": "solid",
            "text": "Shop top 15 promise rings",
            "url": "shopify://collections/top-15-promise-rings",
            "background": "#75AEDC",
            "text_color": "#FFFFFF"
          }
        }
      },
