    "multi_column_4FjN8P": {
      "type": "multi-column",
      "blocks": {
        "image_with_text_8yXecB": {
          "type": "image_with_text",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/2_a68eafb4-72c5-4ced-a4e5-a544a0b6dba9.png",
            "title": "Dating and exclusivity",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "content": "<p>One of the most common meanings is simply: we're committed to each other. A couple may exchange a promise ring after deciding their relationship has become serious or exclusive. Marriage might happen eventually, but it is not necessarily part of the promise being made today.</p><p>For this situation, the right ring finger is a particularly strong option because it communicates romantic commitment without suggesting that a proposal has already happened.</p>",
            "link_url": "shopify://products/marquise-engraved-band-ring",
            "link_text": ""
          }
        },
        "image_with_text_4MCgHk": {
          "type": "image_with_text",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/02_41785a23-f91e-44ad-9881-3468dc5cbd97.jpg",
            "title": "Pre-engagement promise",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "content": "<p>Some promise rings are explicitly pre-engagement rings. The message might be:</p><p>That might be because of age, finances, education, career plans, distance, or simply because the couple does not feel the timing for an engagement is right. In this situation, the left ring finger has the strongest symbolic connection. The ring becomes a visible step in the relationship's progression toward engagement.</p>",
            "link_url": "shopify://products/promise-oval-ring",
            "link_text": ""
          }
        },
        "image_with_text_AjLFtj": {
          "type": "image_with_text",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/OvalClustergold.png",
            "title": "Commitment without marriage",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "content": "<p>A promise ring does not automatically mean that marriage is coming. Some couples are deeply committed to one another but do not want to marry, while others simply do not view marriage as an immediate goal. A promise ring can represent that commitment in its own right.</p><p>The right ring finger or middle finger can work particularly well here because they avoid making the ring appear like a temporary stand-in for an engagement ring.</p>",
            "link_url": "shopify://products/oval-multi-stone-ring",
            "link_text": ""
          }
        },
        "image_with_text_wERBCT": {
          "type": "image_with_text",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/6_56a01833-2f31-4ec1-ba86-4b181b1b88bf.png",
            "title": "Long-distance relationships",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "content": "<p>Promise rings are also sometimes exchanged when couples expect to spend significant time apart. The promise is not necessarily 'we are going to get married.' It may simply mean that distance does not change the commitment. Either ring finger can work, although the right hand may be preferable if the relationship is serious but not explicitly pre-engagement.</p>",
            "link_url": "shopify://products/dainty-promise-band",
            "link_text": ""
          }
        },
        "image_with_text_4trYUA": {
          "type": "image_with_text",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/01_7db28539-6dfd-4bc3-9145-c39d8235390b.jpg",
            "title": "Friendship promise rings",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "content": "<p>Promise rings do not have to be romantic. Friends may exchange rings to represent loyalty, a shared experience, a lifelong friendship, or a commitment to remain connected.</p><p>There is no established friendship promise-ring finger. The middle or index finger is often a useful choice because it clearly separates the ring from conventional engagement jewelry.</p>",
            "link_url": "shopify://products/modern-heirloom-birthstone-ring",
            "link_text": ""
          }
        },
        "image_with_text_mMKVn4": {
          "type": "image_with_text",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/03_91aef889-6c7e-49cb-81de-a5026ed51a05.jpg",
            "title": "Self-promise rings",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "content": "<p>A self-promise ring represents a commitment you make to yourself. That could involve:</p><p>A personal goal, Self-respect, Independence or Personal growth.</p><p>A significant life change or Celebrating an achievement.</p><p>There is no standard finger for a self-promise ring. The middle or index finger is a good starting point because both are highly visible without carrying strong engagement<br/>associations. But this is perhaps the clearest example of a situation where the finger should be entirely your choice.</p>",
            "link_url": "shopify://products/custom-curve-east-west-pear-ring",
            "link_text": ""
          }
        }
      },
