    "image_with_text_R9MHBN": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_nFJBe6": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "text": "Do Men and Women Wear Promise Rings Differently?",
            "heading_tag": "h1"
          }
        },
        "richtext_YjQnzb": {
          "type": "richtext",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>There is no separate promise-ring finger for men. A man can receive a promise ring, give one, or exchange matching or  complementary rings with his partner.</p><p>The same placement principles apply: the left ring finger creates a stronger pre engagement meaning, the right ring finger represents commitment without looking engaged, and the middle or index finger provides a contemporary alternative.</p><p>Men's promise rings may be wider or use materials and designs commonly associated with men's jewelry, but that affects fit and style, not the rules about which finger to use. Couples do not have to wear their rings on the same finger either. One partner might prefer the right ring finger while the other chooses the middle finger. The shared promise matters more than perfect symmetry.</p>"
          }
        },
        "button_LgV8V8": {
